1
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,920


2
00:02:00,413 --> 00:02:01,494
It’s a truly frightening tale.

3
00:02:01,518 --> 00:02:05,797
The late mistress of that house was incredibly wealthy,

4
00:02:05,821 --> 00:02:11,140
yet she was such a miser that she did nothing but torment the poor.

5
00:02:14,450 --> 00:02:17,040
So, you're saying a ghost appears in that house?

6
00:02:17,041 --> 00:02:17,854
Yes.

7
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:21,700
They became a ghost and still linger inside.

8
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:25,780
So, what's that woman's name?

9
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,200
His name is Shainrokku.

10
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:32,300
Where are you off to? It's already dark outside.

11
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:37,640
Besides, you're in the middle of you're studies right now.

12
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:40,200
I'll leave the studying to you.

13
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,281
Make sure you do it right.

14
00:02:41,305 --> 00:02:44,040
Underst— Wait, no way!

15
00:02:45,084 --> 00:02:45,836
Hyah! Out of my way!

16
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,240
Your Highness

17
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,940
Come play with me in the haunted house!

18
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:51,380
You can't leave the castle.

19
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:55,393
Please wait, Lord Sapphire!

20
00:03:03,894 --> 00:03:06,120
Someone stop the Prince!

21
00:03:06,315 --> 00:03:08,060
He went toward the haunted mansion!

22
00:03:11,010 --> 00:03:12,360
Did you hear that, Lord Nylon?

23
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:14,860
Ah, the infamous haunted house.

24
00:03:15,234 --> 00:03:17,230
Follow him and see what he's up to.

25
00:03:17,254 --> 00:03:17,940
Yes, sir.

26
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,700
Wait, but that means I'll have to go inside that haunted house!

27
00:03:22,204 --> 00:03:25,546
Of course! You borrowed money from those ghosts before they died, didn't you? 

28
00:03:25,571 --> 00:03:28,980
You're practically their best customer. Now hurry!

29
00:03:59,416 --> 00:04:02,860
What thick fog... I can barely see a thing.

30
00:04:28,590 --> 00:04:29,590
It went out.

31
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:33,653
What's wrong?

32
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:34,986
Are you scared?

33
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,460
You're hopeless.

34
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,353
I'm not scared at all.

35
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,440
I’m a woman, you know.

36
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:50,075
Now you're fired up! That's the way!

37
00:05:06,370 --> 00:05:07,640
Opal, right here is fine.

38
00:05:07,910 --> 00:05:09,260
I'm staying here tonight.

39
00:05:09,545 --> 00:05:10,700
Come pick me up in the morning.

40
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,820
I'll be fine, really.

41
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,960
Do you think I'd lose to a ghost?

42
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,780
It's fine, you don't need to help.

43
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,300
Go on home, don't worry about me.

44
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,746
Goodbye.

45
00:05:24,945 --> 00:05:26,493
See you tomorrow. Wait!

46
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:40,876
Hey!

47
00:05:41,487 --> 00:05:42,159
Wait!

48
00:05:42,596 --> 00:05:43,093
Hey, wait!

49
00:05:47,664 --> 00:05:49,097
Hey, wait up!

50
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,400
There's no way I can cross this.

51
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:45,820
Actually, that works out fine. Time to go home. The frogs are croaking, so back I go.

52
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,560
Is it this shallow?

53
00:06:55,305 --> 00:06:56,840
Opal

54
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,006
Wait!

55
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,619
Ghost, where are you?

56
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:06,820
Come out!

57
00:07:21,790 --> 00:07:22,920
You think you're guiding me, huh?

58
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,840
Whoa, look at all these books!

59
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:46,326
Amazing!

60
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,760
Don't mind if I do

61
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,879
Looks delicious.

62
00:07:51,626 --> 00:07:54,213
Watch out, watch out. Can't let myself be tricked.

63
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:09,739
I don't need any of that.

64
00:08:14,850 --> 00:08:18,100
I said I don't want it! It's probably just made of stone or mud anyway.

65
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,800
It’s poultry!

66
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:28,800
This is wonderful!

67
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,700
W-Wait a second.

68
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:39,059
How strange.

69
00:08:41,262 --> 00:08:43,846
Hey Ghost, why are you giving me such royal treatment?

70
00:08:44,295 --> 00:08:46,240
Stop doing magic tricks and show yourself.

71
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:48,460
So this is Shainrokku?

72
00:08:49,009 --> 00:08:50,009
She's so pretty.

73
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,520
Who?

74
00:09:02,629 --> 00:09:05,180
Flatterer.

75
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:06,545
It's a ghost!

76
00:09:08,599 --> 00:09:10,000
Indeed I am.

77
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:11,460
A real ghost?

78
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,040
Looks convincing, doesn't it?

79
00:09:14,589 --> 00:09:15,589
You surprised me.

80
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:18,080
I thought ghosts looked much more terrifying.

81
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:21,680
Well, I could do that too.

82
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,780
But that would only turn people off.

83
00:09:24,839 --> 00:09:26,800
Why are you treating me to such a feast?

84
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,720
When you were alive, you were terribly stingy.

85
00:09:30,749 --> 00:09:32,120
Please, go right ahead.

86
00:09:32,285 --> 00:09:35,400
I was the stingiest, greediest soul in the world.

87
00:09:35,513 --> 00:09:42,046
That's why I can't rest in peace, even in death.

88
00:09:43,305 --> 00:09:45,180
I can't ascend to Heaven.

89
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,140
Why don't you just force your way up?

90
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,060
Whenever I call upon Heaven like this...

91
00:09:53,329 --> 00:09:55,979
Look, it's Heaven's guide!

92
00:10:04,030 --> 00:10:06,680
Heaven is calling for me.

93
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:09,680
Looks like you can go to Heaven after all!

94
00:10:11,149 --> 00:10:13,760
No, this is as far as I ever get.

95
00:10:18,869 --> 00:10:20,006
What a strange light.

96
00:10:20,415 --> 00:10:22,700
Ma'am, I'll block the light for you!

97
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,580
Quick, climb up while you can!

98
00:10:24,993 --> 00:10:25,993
Thank you.

99
00:10:31,759 --> 00:10:33,680
Your Highness!

100
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:36,740
Don't worry about me, just get up here!

101
00:10:53,799 --> 00:10:54,799
Hmm... I'm stumped

102
00:10:55,055 --> 00:10:56,700
I see, so this is Hell.

103
00:10:56,845 --> 00:11:01,286
I'm so miserable, I feel like dying.

104
00:11:01,415 --> 00:11:02,720
You're already dead!

105
00:11:03,269 --> 00:11:04,480
Oh, that's right.

106
00:11:07,589 --> 00:11:09,320
But how do you get to Heaven?

107
00:11:10,995 --> 00:11:13,760
Wait, maybe it was the day of your funeral?

108
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,040
No, I never had a funeral.

109
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,640
That's it, Ma'am!

110
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,760
The funeral!

111
00:11:19,359 --> 00:11:21,500
Yeah, you can't hold a ceremony without people.

112
00:11:21,685 --> 00:11:23,740
Ma'am, how many really close friends do you have?

113
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,960
That's right.

114
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,600
I have about three old friends, but...

115
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,720
Three is fine.

116
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:37,020
Tell me where he is—I'll bring him right away.

117
00:11:37,699 --> 00:11:40,720
Why does having a funeral let you go to heaven?

118
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:43,887
If everyone cries and mourns at their funeral, I'm sure even the worst villain 

119
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:47,460
will be mistaken for a good person and let into heaven.

120
00:11:49,049 --> 00:11:51,220
Fine, I'm the villain anyway.

121
00:11:52,259 --> 00:11:54,300
Sorry, I didn't mean it like that.

122
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,620
The address is written right here.

123
00:11:59,479 --> 00:12:01,086
Here, and here... Okay, I got it.

124
00:12:01,395 --> 00:12:03,940
I'll track them down and ask.

125
00:12:22,389 --> 00:12:24,360
Don't be afraid. Drink this.

126
00:12:25,335 --> 00:12:28,240
I lent you money before—did you bring it back?

127
00:12:29,079 --> 00:12:31,820
Geez, even as a ghost, all she thinks about is money.

128
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,220
Even ghosts remember money they're owed!

129
00:12:34,555 --> 00:12:38,020
Oh dear, no, no. I'll never get into heaven talking like this.

130
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,260
Is what you said earlier true?

131
00:12:39,370 --> 00:12:41,960
So if someone cries for you, you can go to heaven?

132
00:12:42,445 --> 00:12:45,040
My, aren't you nasty? Were you eavesdropping?

133
00:12:45,839 --> 00:12:47,320
Then how about I cry for you?

134
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:53,260
Really? I'd be so happy. Please do.

135
00:12:54,209 --> 00:12:56,360
In return, don't press me about the money.

136
00:12:57,539 --> 00:12:59,412
I have a condition of my own.

137
00:12:59,436 --> 00:13:02,160
What, don't tell me you want to borrow money again?

138
00:13:03,146 --> 00:13:04,760
Actually, it's about Sapphire.

139
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,060
Did something happen to the Prince?

140
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:10,900
Actually, I want you to get proof of whether the prince is a girl.

141
00:13:21,199 --> 00:13:22,400
Let's see... it's here.

142
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:23,399
Hello!

143
00:13:23,605 --> 00:13:26,600
Excuse me, is this the house that borrowed money from Madame Shain?

144
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:29,126
Ooh, ow! I’m seeing stars!

145
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:30,620
What a surprise.

146
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:32,606
Sapphire, what's wrong?

147
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,473
Tink, where are you?

148
00:13:35,359 --> 00:13:37,060
Peekaboo! What are you doing?

149
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,560
I'm looking for someone.

150
00:13:39,539 --> 00:13:41,220
There's this poor person, you see.

151
00:13:41,765 --> 00:13:44,020
I'm looking for someone who will cry for them.

152
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:45,673
Oh, I see.

153
00:13:46,039 --> 00:13:47,620
Well, I'll help too.

154
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,200
Tink, you go over there.

155
00:13:49,311 --> 00:13:50,345
Okay.

156
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,340
Hurry up!

157
00:13:55,445 --> 00:13:57,219
We have to help the lady.

158
00:14:00,959 --> 00:14:03,713
Ma'am, have you ever borrowed money from Shainrokku?

159
00:14:04,139 --> 00:14:07,460
I borrowed 50 yen, but I paid it back ages ago. Bye!

160
00:14:12,823 --> 00:14:14,090
Hello?

161
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,200
Yeah, what do you want?

162
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,680
I was having a nice nap, too.

163
00:14:17,965 --> 00:14:19,220
I borrowed money from Shain.

164
00:14:20,409 --> 00:14:22,260
Oh, I borrowed 30 yen, but I haven't paid it back yet.

165
00:14:22,729 --> 00:14:24,480
Then hurry over!

166
00:14:24,511 --> 00:14:25,511
What is it?

167
00:14:25,743 --> 00:14:28,426
They said if you cry for her, you don't have to pay it back.

168
00:14:28,525 --> 00:14:29,525
Really?

169
00:14:29,955 --> 00:14:34,080
What are you doing? Put me down! Put me down, I say! Hey!

170
00:14:34,539 --> 00:14:35,560
Hello, Sir.

171
00:14:36,229 --> 00:14:37,760
Sir, do you know a woman named Shain?

172
00:14:37,761 --> 00:14:40,578
Oh, I sure do. She made me weep, alright.

173
00:14:40,602 --> 00:14:42,386
My goodness... you’re still crying about it even now?

174
00:14:42,495 --> 00:14:43,920
Then come with me and cry!

175
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:46,640
Come on, please cry for her. Won't you?

176
00:14:50,585 --> 00:14:52,600
Delicious!

177
00:14:53,349 --> 00:14:55,840
If it's a funeral like this, I'd come anytime.

178
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:57,220
This is really good!

179
00:15:02,009 --> 00:15:04,194
Now that you've eaten your fill, please cry.

180
00:15:04,219 --> 00:15:05,822
How could I cry for a woman like her?

181
00:15:05,846 --> 00:15:09,155
When she was alive, she wouldn't even give me a single bean!

182
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,500
Outrageous!

183
00:15:10,625 --> 00:15:11,625
What did you say?!

184
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:15,060
You greedy woman!

185
00:15:15,889 --> 00:15:17,120
Well, thanks for the meal.

186
00:15:17,385 --> 00:15:18,385
Time to head home.

187
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:21,040
Wait, cry a little before you go!

188
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:27,280
It's no use.

189
00:15:27,390 --> 00:15:28,390
I ain't cryin'.

190
00:15:28,785 --> 00:15:29,820
Geez!

191
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:32,120
Look here...

192
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:36,020
Instead of the money, she took everything from us—our home, our horses, all of it!

193
00:15:36,973 --> 00:15:39,033
There's no way I can cry like this.

194
00:15:39,290 --> 00:15:40,450
Goodbye.

195
00:15:46,879 --> 00:15:47,900
That's no good.

196
00:15:48,324 --> 00:15:49,500
This won't make them cry.

197
00:15:49,835 --> 00:15:51,646
You'll cry for her, won't you, Miss?

198
00:15:51,875 --> 00:15:53,760
Because she used to work for Shainrokku!

199
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:54,400
No way.

200
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:58,460
She made me work for free for three years and barely even fed me.

201
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:03,240
Someone like that shouldn't go to heaven. She can just wander around forever.

202
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:15,120
Heartless monsters! Every last one of them! Even if I am a ghost, this is just too cruel!

203
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:18,466
I like money. What's wrong with that?

204
00:16:20,369 --> 00:16:21,428
Don't tell me you guys too... 

205
00:16:21,452 --> 00:16:23,260
How boring. Let me go back.

206
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,960
Good idea.

207
00:16:30,929 --> 00:16:32,260
Your Highness, please!

208
00:16:32,525 --> 00:16:33,946
Don't go back.

209
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:47,420
What's wrong?

210
00:16:49,039 --> 00:16:51,125
I'm going back again. To the ghost?

211
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:51,973
Why?

212
00:16:52,409 --> 00:16:54,660
Why? ...What do you think, Opal?

213
00:16:56,689 --> 00:16:59,320
See? Opal agrees with me.

214
00:16:59,805 --> 00:17:01,800
Tink, you go on back to town.

215
00:17:02,115 --> 00:17:03,340
That's no fun.

216
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:04,570
Come on, Opal.

217
00:17:04,952 --> 00:17:06,258
Sapphire!

218
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,908
I'm just a poor, lonely ghost...

219
00:17:11,932 --> 00:17:16,220
That's why I said if you grant my request, I'll cry for you.

220
00:17:16,364 --> 00:17:20,401
But asking me to check if the Prince is a girl... Oh, he came back!

221
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:21,960
Just as I thought.

222
00:17:22,155 --> 00:17:23,412
Mrs. Ghost, handle this well.

223
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,579
I'll be waiting.

224
00:17:24,749 --> 00:17:27,579
Welcome back, Your Highness.

225
00:17:27,704 --> 00:17:29,293
You were so kind earlier...

226
00:17:32,539 --> 00:17:34,540
Now, right this way.

227
00:17:35,879 --> 00:17:37,300
Go ahead, Your Highness.

228
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,160
Wow, how wonderful!

229
00:17:52,104 --> 00:17:53,760
Yes, right over there.

230
00:17:55,239 --> 00:17:57,800
Well? I hope there's a dress you like.

231
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,360
Don't make a fool of me!

232
00:17:59,709 --> 00:18:01,200
These are all women's clothes!

233
00:18:01,824 --> 00:18:03,440
Listen, Lady, I am a prince!

234
00:18:03,774 --> 00:18:05,200
I am a ghost.

235
00:18:05,955 --> 00:18:07,546
If Lord Sapphire sheds a tear, I will become a girl once more. 

236
00:18:07,570 --> 00:18:10,979
I’ll finally know for certain then... whether he is a boy or a girl.

237
00:18:12,009 --> 00:18:13,500
Now then, excuse me for a moment...

238
00:18:14,839 --> 00:18:16,120
Oh dear, it's way too baggy.

239
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:19,320
How about something like this?

240
00:18:20,289 --> 00:18:21,935
Stop it! I said stop!

241
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,700
The mirror is over there.

242
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:26,620
Oh my.

243
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,100
Here you go.

244
00:18:42,864 --> 00:18:46,086
Well, well. What a strange place to meet, Princess Sapphire.

245
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,420
Princess Sapphire?

246
00:18:47,445 --> 00:18:49,986
By the law of this land, a woman cannot become heir to the throne.

247
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:52,659
 Impersonating a man carries the death penalty.

248
00:18:52,685 --> 00:18:53,980
The death penalty?!

249
00:18:55,859 --> 00:18:59,480
Would you prefer to be beheaded, or is hanging more to your liking?

250
00:18:59,632 --> 00:19:01,741
That's absurd, executing such a wonderful person!

251
00:19:01,765 --> 00:19:03,726
It is the law of the Kingdom of Silverland.

252
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:05,140
Don't butt in, ghost!

253
00:19:05,694 --> 00:19:10,706
Once you make up your mind, Grand Duke Duralumin will have you killed. I’ll provide the grandest funeral for you, Princess.

254
00:19:13,629 --> 00:19:16,480
I don't care about the kingdom's laws! Executing such a good person is outrageous!

255
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:19,540
It should be a happy thing to find out she's a princess. What terrible people!

256
00:19:21,039 --> 00:19:22,740
I'm so sorry, Princess Sapphire.

257
00:19:23,129 --> 00:19:27,100
This Nylon is a terrible fellow—you lend him money, and he never pays it back.

258
00:19:28,459 --> 00:19:30,660
Oh, bad-mouthing him woke him right up.

259
00:19:32,119 --> 00:19:33,379
What did I bump into?

260
00:19:33,655 --> 00:19:35,693
Princess, my apologies for keeping you waiting.

261
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:36,700
Princess?

262
00:19:36,819 --> 00:19:38,080
Who are you calling "Princess"?

263
00:19:40,779 --> 00:19:44,120
You are a woman. I just saw it with my own eyes.

264
00:19:44,294 --> 00:19:45,913
Oh, with those eyes?

265
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:47,740
Then take another good look.

266
00:19:50,669 --> 00:19:53,680
When did you find the time to change her clothes, Madame Shain? No doubt about it... this one is a woman!

267
00:19:53,705 --> 00:19:54,420
No.

268
00:19:54,779 --> 00:19:56,600
See? Even the Madame says no.

269
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:57,060
What?

270
00:19:57,639 --> 00:20:00,620
No, Prince Sapphire is a fine prince.

271
00:20:00,775 --> 00:20:01,775
That can't be!

272
00:20:01,946 --> 00:20:02,533
He certainly is.

273
00:20:02,689 --> 00:20:03,920
The dress in this wardrobe...

274
00:20:06,154 --> 00:20:08,520
Dressed as a woman before this mirror...

275
00:20:13,739 --> 00:20:15,200
Madame Shain, how dare you betray me!

276
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:15,880
Just you wait!

277
00:20:15,994 --> 00:20:18,440
I'll post guards around this mansion and let no one in!

278
00:20:18,679 --> 00:20:20,280
Then there'll be no one left to weep for you.

279
00:20:20,524 --> 00:20:24,640
You'll become a ghost in this mansion forever and suffer the torments of hell!

280
00:20:26,294 --> 00:20:27,560
What was that about?

281
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:28,790
Sapphire, you're a woman, aren't you?

282
00:20:33,209 --> 00:20:34,600
Prince Sapphire is...

283
00:20:37,539 --> 00:20:38,826
...a man.

284
00:20:41,065 --> 00:20:42,300
You'll regret this!

285
00:20:44,748 --> 00:20:47,370
Ma'am, why did you waste such a great chance...?

286
00:20:47,394 --> 00:20:49,666
I don't know. I don't understand it myself.

287
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:52,460
Light!

288
00:20:52,719 --> 00:20:54,340
It looks like you’re going to Heaven, Ma'am.

289
00:20:59,369 --> 00:21:01,400
I'll give it a try. Thank you, Prince.

290
00:21:05,109 --> 00:21:06,260
Watch out, Ma'am!

291
00:21:08,769 --> 00:21:11,160
Help! Help!

292
00:21:12,999 --> 00:21:14,820
Guess it didn't work out after all, Ma'am.

293
00:21:15,024 --> 00:21:21,020
Poor Prince... I hate Heaven. Why do Heaven and Hell even exist in the afterlife?

294
00:21:21,044 --> 00:21:22,840
If I just died, then nothing...

295
00:21:24,499 --> 00:21:25,540
What's that sound?

296
00:21:29,169 --> 00:21:30,420
The ghost is over there!

297
00:21:30,599 --> 00:21:32,060
Set fire to the room and burn it down!

298
00:21:34,174 --> 00:21:35,620
Oh, they're trying to burn down the mansion!

299
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:36,960
I won't let them!

300
00:21:38,389 --> 00:21:39,580
Damn those men!

301
00:21:39,759 --> 00:21:41,433
Men, set fires everywhere!

302
00:21:43,209 --> 00:21:44,360
Come on, burn! Burn!

303
00:21:49,839 --> 00:21:53,520
It's useless to burn it to ashes, Nylon.

304
00:21:53,709 --> 00:21:55,893
Damn it, what are you doing? Burn it down!

305
00:21:56,729 --> 00:21:58,160
Nylon, stop setting fires!

306
00:21:58,270 --> 00:21:59,270
It's an order from the Prince!

307
00:21:59,909 --> 00:22:01,240
No, you are no prince.

308
00:22:01,340 --> 00:22:03,180
Lady Sapphire, you are a woman.

309
00:22:03,674 --> 00:22:05,693
Quick, seize Princess Sapphire!

310
00:22:07,875 --> 00:22:09,286
Alright! If that's the case, I’ll definitely put this fire out!

311
00:22:09,364 --> 00:22:10,666
Ma'am, please put out the fire!

312
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,280
She's in danger!

313
00:22:26,279 --> 00:22:27,620
This mansion is done for.

314
00:22:28,449 --> 00:22:30,280
Now then... you’re about to become a beggar ghost!

315
00:22:30,649 --> 00:22:31,649
A beggar ghost!

316
00:22:33,146 --> 00:22:34,500
Hey, get your hands off!

317
00:22:34,629 --> 00:22:36,140
Ma'am, it's dangerous over there!

318
00:22:39,969 --> 00:22:41,520
Ma'am, so this is where you were!

319
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:42,660
Let's get out of here, quick!

320
00:22:42,779 --> 00:22:46,620
I'm a ghost, so I'm fine. I'm just exhausted...

321
00:22:47,659 --> 00:22:48,680
Your Highness, look out!

322
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:50,600
Please, run away!

323
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:51,820
Don't worry about me.

324
00:22:52,459 --> 00:22:53,720
I'm sorry for all the trouble...

325
00:22:54,044 --> 00:22:56,000
I've given up now.

326
00:22:56,679 --> 00:22:58,100
Are you really okay with not going to Heaven?

327
00:22:58,190 --> 00:22:59,833
It's fine. Please, just run!

328
00:22:59,949 --> 00:23:02,100
The mansion will burn down any second.

329
00:23:02,454 --> 00:23:05,440
Nylon and his men are after your life, so please be careful.

330
00:23:05,754 --> 00:23:07,080
You care about me that much...?

331
00:23:08,113 --> 00:23:09,250
Ah, Ma'am!

332
00:23:09,274 --> 00:23:11,760
Lord Sapphire, please be careful...

333
00:23:12,259 --> 00:23:14,240
To think she worried about me this much...

334
00:23:15,054 --> 00:23:16,200
Thank you, Ma'am.

335
00:23:21,759 --> 00:23:23,720
The fire... The fire stopped! What happened?

336
00:23:23,969 --> 00:23:28,200
Prince Sapphire, because you wept for me, I can go to heaven.

337
00:23:28,324 --> 00:23:30,566
Get outside while the flames have stopped!

338
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:31,640
Hurry!

339
00:23:44,220 --> 00:23:46,000
It's Prince Sapphire's ghost!

340
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:46,793
Nylon!

341
00:23:47,033 --> 00:23:48,920
Well well, my Prince, you managed to escape.

342
00:23:49,119 --> 00:23:51,246
By the way, what happened to Shain's ghost?

343
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:59,120
Look. Madame Shain is ascending to Heaven.

344
00:24:04,729 --> 00:24:06,979
Goodbye, Ma'am!

345
00:24:07,003 --> 00:24:09,003

